      },
      "message": "docs(turning): record why the laid flank pass ends stay short of D\n\nA control running G76 ends every flank pass at D. The kernel lays a\nshallower pass short of D by its flank offset. The flank-angle refusal\nkeeps that run-out inside the root pass's V, so the output is safe.\nLaying a partial helical arc to D would put an arc end off the\nmeridian. That breaks the holder and rapid laws, both lathe posts'\nhalf-turn contracts and the two thread verdicts, for a P7 gain.\n\nThe pin keeps its assertion and now names the decision.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nFixes #1896",
